---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Aeldari Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to the Aeldari? Learn the tragic lore of the Fall, how the elite fast army plays, how to paint curved armor, and what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">👁️</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Aeldari</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            Once the masters of the galaxy. Now a dying race haunted by what they became. 
            The Aeldari are fast, psychic, devastatingly precise — and every death 
            is one they can never replace. The most tragic faction in 40k, 
            and the one with the most beautiful models.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Elite & Fast</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-red-400">Complex</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160–$240</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Aeldari?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          Before humanity discovered fire, the Aeldari ruled the galaxy. 
          Their civilization was ancient when the Milky Way was young — 
          psychic beings of extraordinary intelligence and grace, 
          whose empire touched every corner of known space. 
          They built the Webway: a network of tunnels through sub-reality connecting their worlds, 
          invisible and instantaneous. For millions of years, nothing threatened them.
        </p>
        <p>
          That was their undoing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Without struggle, the Aeldari turned inward. Their society fractured into 
          decadence — pleasure cults, cruelty, obsession, excess. 
          Their psychic nature meant that every emotion they felt resonated in the Warp. 
          Across ten thousand years, their collective depravity built a presence in the immaterium — 
          a vast, growing thing made of their worst impulses. 
          Then, approximately ten thousand years ago, it was born.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Slaanesh</strong> — the Chaos God of excess, sensation, 
          and pleasure — tore itself into existence in a psychic cataclysm that 
          consumed the Aeldari empire in an instant. 
          The Eye of Terror opened where their heart worlds once were. 
          Billions died. Their civilization, built across millions of years, 
          ended in a single screaming moment called <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">the Fall</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The survivors were those already traveling the stars on massive city-ships called 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Craftworlds</strong> — and those disciplined enough 
          to have kept themselves separate from the corruption. 
          Now there are perhaps millions of Aeldari left in a galaxy of trillions. 
          They know their species is dying. Every death is irreplaceable. 
          And Slaanesh still hungers for their souls — which is why every Aeldari 
          wears a Spirit Stone to capture their consciousness at death, 
          preserving it in the Wraithbone matrix of their Craftworld rather than 
          letting it be consumed.
        </p>
        <p>
          They fight because they have to. They win because they've had ten thousand years 
          to practice, and they can't afford to lose.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Craftworld choice -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">Choose your Craftworld</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Each surviving Craftworld has its own culture, colors, and battlefield doctrine. 
        This is the most important aesthetic decision you'll make.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        {[
          {
            name: 'Ulthwé',
            colors: 'Black & Gold',
            swatch1: 'bg-gray-900',
            swatch2: 'bg-yellow-500',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: 'The most powerful psyker Craftworld — Ulthwé sits near the Eye of Terror and has spent ten millennia fighting Chaos. Dark, brooding black armor with gold trim. One of the easiest schemes to execute and incredibly striking on the table.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Iyanden',
            colors: 'Yellow & Blue',
            swatch1: 'bg-yellow-400',
            swatch2: 'bg-blue-700',
            painting: 'Hard',
            paintColor: 'text-red-400',
            desc: "Devastated by Tyranids — most of Iyanden's population are dead, their spirits preserved in Wraith constructs that now make up the bulk of the army. Ghost warriors, wraithguard, wraithlords. Beautiful yellow and blue scheme but yellow is notoriously difficult to paint evenly.",
          },
          {
            name: 'Saim-Hann',
            colors: 'Red & White',
            swatch1: 'bg-red-600',
            swatch2: 'bg-gray-100',
            painting: 'Medium',
            paintColor: 'text-yellow-400',
            desc: 'Wild Riders — Saim-Hann is the cavalry Craftworld, famous for fast Jetbikes and aggressive hit-and-run tactics. Bold red with white and black detailing. Passionate, fierce, and completely ignoring the structured Path system.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Alaitoc',
            colors: 'Blue & Yellow',
            swatch1: 'bg-blue-600',
            swatch2: 'bg-yellow-400',
            painting: 'Medium',
            paintColor: 'text-yellow-400',
            desc: 'Rangers and scouts — Alaitoc produces more Outcasts (Aeldari who walk away from the rigid Path system) than any other Craftworld. Many become Rangers, sniping from impossible distances. Blue and yellow scheme with a tactical, infiltration-focused playstyle.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Biel-Tan',
            colors: 'Green & White',
            swatch1: 'bg-green-700',
            swatch2: 'bg-gray-100',
            painting: 'Medium',
            paintColor: 'text-yellow-400',
            desc: "The most aggressive Craftworld — Biel-Tan believes the Aeldari empire can be rebuilt and pursues that goal through war. Heavy on Aspect Warriors, especially Dire Avengers. Dark green armor with white and bone detailing.",
          },
        ].map(cw => (
          <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="flex gap-1 flex-shrink-0">
                <div class={`w-3 h-12 rounded-l ${cw.swatch1}`}></div>
                <div class={`w-3 h-12 rounded-r ${cw.swatch2}`}></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flex-1">
                <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-3 mb-1">
                  <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg">{cw.name}</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">{cw.colors}</span>
                  <span class={`text-xs font-semibold ${cw.paintColor}`}>Painting: {cw.painting}</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">{cw.desc}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-5 italic">
        Beginner recommendation: Ulthwé. Black + gold is fast, forgiving, and looks incredible. 
        Avoid Iyanden until you're comfortable with yellow.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          Aeldari are an <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">elite, mobile army</strong>. 
          You will have fewer models than almost any opponent — but each one hits harder, 
          moves faster, and does something specific extremely well. 
          The army lives or dies by positioning and target priority.
        </p>
        <p>
          The core of the army is <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Aspect Warriors</strong> — 
          specialized warrior temples, each dedicated to one facet of war. 
          Fire Dragons destroy vehicles and nothing else. 
          Howling Banshees hit so fast enemies can't react to a charge. 
          Dark Reapers stand back and delete units with precision artillery fire. 
          You don't take generalists — you take specialists and deploy them against 
          exactly the right target.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Aeldari are also the most <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">psychic</strong> faction. 
          Multiple powerful Farseers and Warlocks provide crucial buffs, 
          debuffs, and damage that other armies simply don't have access to.
        </p>
        <p>
          The honest caveat: this is a <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">high skill floor army</strong>. 
          Because your models are fragile (individually expensive in points, 
          often with poor armor saves), mistakes are punishing. 
          A misdeployed squad of Howling Banshees that gets shot before they can charge 
          is ten models gone — and ten models you genuinely feel. 
          This isn't the right first faction if you're still learning the core rules. 
          But if you have some games under your belt, the ceiling is tremendous.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Aeldari are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You want the most beautiful models in the game</li>
            <li>✓ You love the tragic, ancient civilization lore</li>
            <li>✓ You want a high-skill, high-reward army to master</li>
            <li>✓ You want strong psychic abilities</li>
            <li>✓ You want speed and precision over brute force</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You're still learning the game — mistakes are expensive</li>
            <li>✗ You want a horde or lots of bodies</li>
            <li>✗ You want a simple, forgiving playstyle</li>
            <li>✗ You want the grimdark human-scale story</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Aeldari</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-4 text-lg">Using Ulthwé (black + gold) — the most beginner-friendly Craftworld.</p>
      <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] mb-10 leading-relaxed">
        Aeldari armor is curved and elegant — the opposite of the angular slabs you see on Space Marines. 
        This means contrast paints and drybrushing work differently here. 
        The curved surfaces reward a careful edge highlight, but even a simple wash and drybrush 
        looks good. Ulthwé forgives a lot — dark colors hide imperfections.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spray Abaddon Black</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Black primer over the whole model. Ulthwé's dark armor is your base. Make sure you get full coverage — gaps in black primer show badly on dark models.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Drybrush Mechanicus Standard Grey on armor panels</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A medium grey drybrush catches all the raised curves and edges of the armor, creating instant highlight without touching a fine brush to every edge.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Retributor Armour on all gold trim</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Helmet crests, shoulder pad rims, chest gems, weapon casings. The gold contrast against dark armor is the signature Ulthwé look — take your time here, it's worth it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Reikland Fleshshade over the gold</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A brown-gold wash that flows into the recesses of the trim and enriches the gold tone. Takes it from flat metallic paint to genuine antique gold.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spirit stone gems — Tesseract Glow or Waystone Green</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Every Aeldari model has spirit stones — small gems on the chest or helmet. A dab of Tesseract Glow (green OSL technical paint) in the recess creates a glowing gem effect instantly. This detail transforms the model.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Nuln Oil in recesses, base the model</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A thin Nuln Oil wash into the deepest recesses of the armor panels adds the final depth. Base with a dark stone texture paint and a sparse tuft — sparse because Aeldari feel ancient, not overgrown.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">The edge highlight upgrade</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The drybrushed grey gets you 80% of the way. The last 20% — 
          and what makes Aeldari look truly spectacular — is a thin edge highlight 
          of Administratum Grey along the sharpest armor curves. 
          This requires a fine detail brush and a steady hand, but it's not as hard as it looks. 
          Practice on one model first, then decide if you want to do it on the whole army. 
          The result is worth it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">One box. Learn the models and the scheme before anything else.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Aeldari Corsairs</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Includes Kharseth (a Corsair Prince leader), a Wave Serpent (iconic transport 
          that also fires weapons), 5 Corsair Skyreavers, and 10 Corsair Voidreavers 
          (buildable as Voidscarred). A mobile, elite Corsair raiding force — fast, 
          aggressive, and entirely distinct from the Craftworld Guardians of older boxes.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.games-workshop.com/en-US/Craftworlds-Combat-Patrol"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Buy from Games Workshop →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$65 · choose based on your playstyle</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Howling Banshees or Fire Dragons</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Your first Aspect Warrior squad defines your playstyle. 
          Howling Banshees are fast melee specialists — terrifying in close combat. 
          Fire Dragons are the best anti-tank unit in the faction — 
          they delete vehicles without breaking a sweat. 
          Pick whichever role feels missing from your Combat Patrol.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.games-workshop.com/en-US/Aeldari"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Browse Aeldari on Games Workshop →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need (Ulthwé scheme)</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Abaddon Black Spray', use: 'Primer and armor base coat', required: true },
            { name: 'Mechanicus Standard Grey', use: 'Drybrush on armor curves', required: true },
            { name: 'Retributor Armour', use: 'Gold trim — helmet, shoulder rims, gems', required: true },
            { name: 'Reikland Fleshshade', use: 'Wash over gold trim', required: true },
            { name: 'Tesseract Glow', use: 'Spirit stone gems', required: true },
            { name: 'Nuln Oil', use: 'Recess wash on armor panels', required: true },
            { name: 'Administratum Grey', use: 'Edge highlight on sharpest armor curves', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">~$38 for the full set. The spirit stone step (Tesseract Glow) is worth every penny — it's the detail that makes the models feel Aeldari.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Aeldari Corsairs', cost: '~$160', note: 'Kharseth, Wave Serpent, Skyreavers, Voidreavers' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (6)', cost: '~$38', note: 'Spray + grey + gold + wash + glow + Nuln' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Dark stone texture + sparse tufts' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Fine detail parts need precise gluing' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$235</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Aspect Warrior squads (~$50–65 each) are the natural second purchase. 
        Pick one that fills a gap in your patrol — Fire Dragons if you need anti-tank, 
        Howling Banshees if you want a melee option.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">We were here before you. We will outlast you.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Choose your Craftworld, paint with patience, and learn your Aspect Warriors. 
        The Aeldari reward mastery more than any other faction — and they're worth mastering.
      </p>
